<!doctype html>
<!-- {{ ansible_managed }} -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Using your Mac from the office PCs</title>
<style>
  :root { --text: #1d1d1f; --muted: #6e6e73; --line: #d2d2d7; --accent: #0066cc; --box: #f5f5f7; }
  body { font: 16px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
         color: var(--text); max-width: 46rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; margin-bottom: .2rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: .3rem; }
  .lead { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0; }
  ol li, ul li { margin: .35rem 0; }
  code, kbd { font: .92em ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; background: var(--box);
              border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; padding: .05rem .3rem; }
  pre { background: var(--box); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: .7rem 1rem;
        overflow-x: auto; font: .95em ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .note { background: var(--box); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding: .6rem 1rem; border-radius: 4px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  td { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: .5rem .4rem; vertical-align: top; }
  td:first-child { font-weight: 600; width: 38%; }
  @media print { body { margin: 0; } h2 { break-after: avoid; } .note, pre, tr { break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Using your Mac from the office PCs</h1>
<p class="lead">At any office PC, its keyboard, mouse and screens work your own Mac, wherever it is
in the office. You no longer need to bring a screen, keyboard or cables.</p>

<h2>Setting up (once)</h2>
<p>You need: a Mac with macOS 14 or newer, its password, and the office network. You get two
files: this manual and <code>{{ netstation_mac_handout_script_name }}</code>.</p>
<ol>
  <li>Save <code>{{ netstation_mac_handout_script_name }}</code> in your <strong>Downloads</strong> folder.</li>
  <li>Open <strong>Terminal</strong> (Cmd+Space, type <em>Terminal</em>, press Enter). iTerm or another
    terminal app works too.</li>
  <li>Type this and press Enter:
    <pre>bash ~/Downloads/{{ netstation_mac_handout_script_name }}</pre></li>
  <li>Do what it says. It asks for your Mac's password once; you don't see it while you type.
    <ul>
      <li>When RustDesk opens, click <strong>Install</strong> in its sidebar and enter your password. RustDesk then
        runs in the background whenever your Mac starts, so the office PC can reach your Mac without opening
        RustDesk first, also when it's locked. Rather not? Press Enter in the terminal to skip it, and open RustDesk
        yourself before you use your Mac from the office PC.</li>
      <li>In RustDesk, click the buttons for <strong>Screen Recording</strong> and <strong>Accessibility</strong>,
        and switch RustDesk on in both lists in System Settings. Press Enter in the terminal after each one.</li>
    </ul></li>
  <li>At the end it shows your <strong>RustDesk ID</strong>, nine digits: you type it at the office PC. No need to
    remember it; it's always in RustDesk's window.</li>
</ol>
<p class="note">Got a new version of the script? Run it again the same way. It updates the apps and
keeps your settings.</p>

<h2>Every day</h2>
<ol>
  <li>On your Mac, open <strong>{{ netstation_mac_office_mode_name }}</strong> (Cmd+Space, type
    <em>{{ netstation_mac_office_mode_name }}</em>, press Enter) and click <em>{{ netstation_mac_handout_messages.switch_on }}</em>.
    {% if netstation_mac_office_builtin_off %}Your Mac's own screen goes dark: you now see it on the office PC.{% else %}Your Mac's
    own screen stays on; the office PC usually shows it on its left screen.{% endif %}</li>
  <li>At the office PC, double-click the <strong>{{ netstation_remote_mac_icon_name | default('Mac') }}</strong> icon on the desktop and type your RustDesk ID.
    It's in RustDesk's window on your Mac.</li>
  <li>Allow the connection, in either of two ways; follow what your Mac or the office PC shows:
    <ul>
      <li>on your Mac, click <strong>Accept</strong> in RustDesk, or</li>
      <li>at the office PC, type the password RustDesk shows on your Mac. It changes after each session.</li>
    </ul></li>
</ol>
<p>While {{ netstation_mac_office_mode_name }} is on, your Mac stays awake. macOS then lists
{{ netstation_mac_office_mode_name }} as an app running in the background; that's right, and it also tells you
it's still on. Keep it on the office network.
With the charger connected you can close the lid once you're connected: your Mac keeps working, and the
office PC then shows exactly the two office screens. If the connection drops, open the lid briefly to allow
it again; with the lid closed you can't see the password or the Accept button.</p>
<p>On the office PC, the key next to the space bar works as <kbd>Cmd</kbd>, as on a Mac keyboard.
To stop, close the RustDesk windows with the small bar at the top of the screen.</p>
<p>When you leave, or at home: open <strong>{{ netstation_mac_office_mode_name }}</strong> again. It switches the
office screens off{% if netstation_mac_office_builtin_off %} and your Mac's own screen back on{% endif %}.</p>
{% if netstation_mac_office_builtin_off %}
<p class="note">Your Mac's screen stays dark and you can't see it? Press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd>,
type <em>{{ netstation_mac_office_mode_name }}</em> and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>If something doesn't work</h2>
<table>
  <tr><td>You see your Mac, but the mouse and keyboard do nothing</td>
      <td>RustDesk lacks <em>Accessibility</em>. Switch it on in System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security
      &gt; Accessibility, then quit and reopen RustDesk.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>The screen stays black</td>
      <td>RustDesk lacks <em>Screen Recording</em>: same place, under Screen Recording.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>"ID does not exist" or it can't connect</td>
      <td>Is your Mac on, awake and on the office network, and does RustDesk say <em>Ready</em> at the bottom
      of its window? Otherwise run the setup script again.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>"Key mismatch"</td><td>Run the setup script again.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>It lags</td><td>Usually the Wi-Fi. A network cable (a USB-C adapter) fixes it.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Windows end up on screens you can't see</td>
      <td>{{ netstation_mac_office_mode_name }} is still on: open it again to switch it off.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>For IT</h2>
<p>RustDesk on the Mac uses the office's own server, under Settings &gt; Network &gt; ID/Relay server:</p>
<table>
  <tr><td>ID server</td><td><code>{{ netstation_remote_mac_server_address }}</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td>Relay server</td><td>(empty)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Key</td><td><code>{{ netstation_rustdesk_public_key }}</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td>Versions</td><td>RustDesk {{ netstation_mac_rustdesk_version }},
      SimpleDisplay {{ netstation_mac_simpledisplay_version }}</td></tr>
</table>

</body>
</html>
